{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792510393,"nonce":"R3lasgjBLEwJIG5EfjiItz+8hr8=","title":"Preserve circle, ellipse and polygon clips on raw RGBA images","message":"Child of 369499d9d754d8353823d4eb9ff5ff76e5469007b2983e58b3a677f88b5bbc6c.\n\nRaw image emission discards get_clip_data's ClipType. Circle and ellipse payloads are interpreted as corner radii or ignored when there is no rectangular scissor; polygon vertex counts/offsets are also interpreted as corner radii. Carry these supported native clip shapes through image-only foreground projection, motion and composite scratch ownership, ordered layers and tight-origin rendering. Preserve the native polygon frame and fill rule, and invalidate scratch caches when clip metadata changes.\n\nUse self-contained per-image clip rows with the existing image pipeline so payloads survive batch drains and merging without auxiliary-pointer rebasing. Verify independent offscreen pixel controls and all native storage modes. Ordinary rectangular/rounded clips and empty-clip rejection already work. Native ClipShape::Path currently falls back to no clipping for every primitive; path clipping and broader clip-stack/transform semantics are outside this slice. Do not change the shared ClipPath ABI or CSS keywords.","files":null}]}